      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "60e617149bf11f73e52db8f1",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "In your Advanced Safety settings, you can filter out avatar performance and \"Perf Block\" them. I don't think that Udon programming can interact with VRChat's avatar API.\nTo mitigate some worries about unoptimized avatars in a world, it's healthy to encourage avatar creators to consider re-uploading their avatar with better performance. Some dance club worlds will have signs heavily recommending users to change to an avatar that is not 'Poor' or worse with performance before going in.\nIf you're a world creator, I can recommend these tips to help other users decrease lag. However, I shouldn't worry too much, since VRChat gave every user the tools necessary to hide avatars that are too laggy, whether it's automatic via Safety settings, or manually hiding an avatar in the Quick Menu.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
